    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0130" n="31" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg31"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Peace Personnel/279: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hull</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-14T17:00:00-05:00">November 14, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. The American Consul at Geneva reported on November 10 that he was told by the
                    Argentine representative at Geneva that the latter had taken up with the
                    Secretariat the possibility of a League observer attending the Conference. The
                    Argentine representative had received information that Sweetser<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d31-f1"/> was a candidate and he felt that <pb facs="0131" n="32"
                        xml:id="pg32"/> he should suggest that Sweetser would not be entirely
                    acceptable to Argentina.</p>
                <p>The Argentine representative confirmed to the American Consul that although the
                    Argentine delegation, during the Assembly, had generally favored the sending of
                    a League observer to the Conference, it was now the impression that Buenos Aires
                    would not take the initiative in such a development.</p>
                <p>The American Consul has been authoritatively advised that Avenol<anchor n="43"
                        xml:id="d31-f2"/> informed the political section of the Secretariat of his
                    decision not to take any action with respect to sending an observer to Buenos
                    Aires unless a formal invitation in that sense is received by the League.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d31-f1" n="42" xml:id="d31-f1-content">
                <p>Arthur Sweetser, attached to the office of the Secretary-General, League of
                    Nations, with rank of director.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d31-f2" n="43" xml:id="d31-f2-content">
                <p>Joseph A. Avenol, Secretary-General, League of Nations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
